From d5e02f0293f966f1c2d6618d4178809a2365fd75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:40:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] opengl: share the persistent vertex cache with the OpenGL
 renderer

The cache bookkeeping moves to video_core/vertex_region_cache.h. OpenGL keeps game vertex buffers
in six 32 MiB GL buffers (glBufferSubData orders the updates against earlier draws, so recycling
needs no fence) and points the attributes into them; uncached loaders keep the per-draw copy,
now bounded to the memory region like the Vulkan path.
